#: src/git.md:3
msgid "Git"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed has built-in Git support that lets you manage version control without "
"leaving the editor. The Git Panel shows your working tree state, staging "
"area, and branch information. Changes you make on the command line are "
"reflected immediately in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:7
msgid ""
"For operations that Zed doesn't support natively, you can use the integrated "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:9
msgid "Git Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:11
msgid ""
"The Git Panel shows the state of your working tree and Git's staging area."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:13
msgid ""
"You can open the Git Panel using <code class=\"hljs\">git panel: toggle "
"focus</code>, or by clicking the Git icon in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:15
msgid ""
"In the panel you can see the state of your project at a glance: which "
"repository and branch are active, what files have changed and the current "
"staging state of each file."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:17
msgid ""
"Zed monitors your repository so that changes you make on the command line "
"are instantly reflected."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:19
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:21
msgid ""
"Open the Settings Editor (`Cmd+,` on macOS, `Ctrl+,` on Linux/Windows) to "
"customize Git behavior. Settings are spread across two pages:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:23
msgid ""
"**Panels > Git Panel**: Panel position, tree vs flat view, status display "
"style"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:24
msgid "**Version Control**: Gutter indicators, inline blame, hunk styles"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:26
msgid "Moving the Git Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:28
msgid ""
"By default, the Git Panel docks on the left. Go to **Panels > Git Panel** "
"and change **Git Panel Dock** to move it to the right or bottom."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:30
msgid "Switching to Tree View"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:32
msgid ""
"The Git Panel shows a flat list of changed files by default. To see files "
"organized by folder hierarchy instead, toggle **Tree View** in the panel's "
"context menu, or enable it in **Panels > Git Panel**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:34
msgid "Inline Blame"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:36
msgid ""
"Zed shows Git blame information on the current line. To turn this off or add "
"a delay before it appears, go to **Version Control > Inline Git Blame**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:38
msgid "Hiding the Gutter Indicators"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:40
msgid ""
"The colored bars in the gutter that show added, modified, and deleted lines "
"can be hidden. Go to **Version Control > Git Gutter** and set **Visibility** "
"to \"Hide\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:42
msgid "Commit Message Line Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:44
msgid ""
"Zed wraps commit messages at 72 characters (a Git convention). To change "
"this, search for \"Git Commit\" in Settings and adjust **Preferred Line "
"Length**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:46
msgid "Project Diff"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:48
msgid ""
"You can see all of the changes captured by Git in Zed by opening the Project "
"Diff (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-g d\\|ctrl-g d</kbd>), accessible via "
"the <code class=\"hljs\">git: diff</code> action in the Command Palette or "
"the Git Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:50
msgid ""
"All of the changes displayed in the Project Diff behave exactly the same as "
"any other multibuffer: they are all editable excerpts of files."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:52
msgid ""
"You can stage or unstage each hunk as well as a whole file by hitting the "
"buttons on the tab bar or their corresponding keybindings."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:54
msgid "Word Diff Highlighting"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:56
msgid ""
"By default, Zed highlights changed words within modified lines to make it "
"easier to spot exactly what changed. To disable this globally, open the "
"Settings Editor and go to **Languages & Tools > Miscellaneous**, then turn "
"off **Word Diff Enabled**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:58
msgid ""
"To disable word diff for specific languages only, add this to your settings."
"json:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:62
msgid "\"languages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:63
msgid "\"Markdown\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:64
msgid "\"word_diff_enabled\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:70
msgid "Diff View Styles"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:72
msgid ""
"Zed displays diffs in two modes: **split** (side-by-side comparison) or "
"**unified** (inline changes). Split view is the default."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:74
msgid "Changing the diff view"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:76
msgid ""
"Open the Settings Editor (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,\\|ctrl-,</kbd>) "
"and search for \"diff view style\". Select either **Split** or **Unified**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:78
msgid "To change the default, add this to your `settings.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:82
msgid "\"diff_view_style\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:82
msgid "\"unified\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:86
msgid ""
"See [Configuring Zed](./configuring-zed.md) for more about the Settings "
"Editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:88
msgid "Split vs unified"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:90
msgid ""
"**Split**: Shows the original and modified versions side by side. Useful for "
"comparing file structure or reviewing large changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:91
msgid ""
"**Unified**: Shows changes inline with additions and deletions in a single "
"view. Useful for focusing on specific line changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:93
msgid ""
"You can switch between modes at any time. Your preference applies to "
"[Project Diff](#project-diff), [File History](#file-history), and [Stash "
"Diff View](#stash-diff-view). These diff views function as [multibuffers](./"
"multibuffers.md), allowing you to edit multiple excerpts simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:95
msgid "File History"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:97
msgid ""
"File History shows the commit history for an individual file. Each entry "
"displays the commit's author, timestamp, and message. Selecting a commit "
"opens a diff view filtered to show only the changes made to that file in "
"that commit."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:99
msgid "To view File History:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:101
msgid ""
"Right-click on a file in the Project Panel and select \"View File History\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:102
msgid "Right-click on a file in the Git Panel and select \"View File History\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:103
msgid "Right-click on an editor tab and select \"View File History\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:104
msgid "Use the Command Palette and search for \"file history\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:106
msgid "Fetch, Push, and Pull"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:108
msgid ""
"Fetch, push, or pull from your Git repository in Zed via the buttons "
"available on the Git Panel or via the Command Palette by looking at the "
"respective actions: <code class=\"hljs\">git: fetch</code>, <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: push</code>, and <code class=\"hljs\">git: pull</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:110
msgid "Push Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:112
msgid ""
"Zed respects Git's push configuration. When pushing, Zed checks the "
"following in order:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:114
msgid "`pushRemote` configured for the current branch"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:115
msgid "`remote.pushDefault` in your Git config"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:116
msgid "The branch's tracking remote"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:118
msgid ""
"This matches Git's standard behavior, so if you've configured `pushRemote` "
"or `pushDefault` in your `.gitconfig` or via `git config`, Zed will use "
"those settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:120
msgid "Remotes"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:122
msgid ""
"When your repository has multiple remotes, Zed shows a remote selector in "
"the Git Panel. Click the remote button next to push/pull to choose which "
"remote to use for that operation."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:124
msgid "Staging Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:126
msgid ""
"Zed has two primary staging workflows, using either the Project Diff or the "
"panel directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:128
msgid "Using the Project Diff"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:130
msgid ""
"In the Project Diff view, you can focus on each hunk and stage them "
"individually by clicking on the tab bar buttons or via the keybindings <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: stage and next</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-y\\|"
"alt-y</kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:132
msgid ""
"Similarly, stage all hunks at the same time with the <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: stage all</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-ctrl-y\\|"
"ctrl-space</kbd>) keybinding and then immediately commit with <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: commit</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter\\|"
"ctrl-enter</kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:134
msgid "Using the Git Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:136
msgid ""
"From the panel, you can simply type a commit message and hit the commit "
"button, or <code class=\"hljs\">git: commit</code>. This will automatically "
"stage all tracked files (indicated by a `[·]` in the entry's checkbox) and "
"commit them."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:140
msgid ""
"Entries can be staged using each individual entry's checkbox. All changes "
"can be staged using the button at the top of the panel, or <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: stage all</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:144
msgid "Committing"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:146
msgid "Zed offers two commit textareas:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:148
msgid ""
"The first one is available right at the bottom of the Git Panel. Hitting "
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter\\|ctrl-enter</kbd> immediately commits "
"all of your staged changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:149
msgid ""
"The second is available via the action <code class=\"hljs\">git: expand "
"commit editor</code> or via hitting the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-"
"escape\\|</kbd> while focused in the Git Panel commit textarea."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:151
msgid "Undoing a Commit"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:153
msgid ""
"As soon as you commit in Zed, in the Git Panel, you'll see a bar right under "
"the commit textarea, which will show the recently submitted commit. In "
"there, you can use the \"Uncommit\" button, which performs the `git reset "
"HEADˆ--soft` command."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:156
msgid "Configuring Commit Line Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:158
msgid ""
"By default, Zed sets the commit line length to `72` but it can be configured "
"in your local `settings.json` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:160
msgid ""
"Find more information about setting the `preferred-line-length` in the "
"[Configuration](#configuration) section."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:162
msgid "Branch Management"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:164
msgid "Creating and Switching Branches"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:166
msgid ""
"Create a new branch using <code class=\"hljs\">git: branch</code> or switch "
"to an existing branch using <code class=\"hljs\">git: switch</code> or <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: checkout branch</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:168
msgid "Deleting Branches"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:170
msgid ""
"To delete a branch, open the branch switcher with <code class=\"hljs\">git: "
"switch</code>, find the branch you want to delete, and use the delete "
"option. Zed will confirm before deleting to prevent accidental data loss."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:172
msgid ""
"**Note:** You cannot delete the branch you currently have checked out. "
"Switch to a different branch first."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:174
msgid "Merge Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:176
msgid ""
"When you encounter merge conflicts after a merge, rebase, or pull, Zed "
"highlights the conflicting regions in your files and displays resolution "
"buttons above each conflict."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:178
msgid "Viewing Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:180
msgid ""
"Conflicting files appear in the Git Panel with a warning icon. You can also "
"see conflicts in the Project Diff view, where each conflict region is "
"highlighted:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:182
msgid "Changes from your current branch are highlighted in green"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:183
msgid "Changes from the incoming branch are highlighted in blue"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:185
msgid "Resolving Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:187
msgid "Each conflict shows three buttons:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:189
msgid ""
"**Use \\[branch-name\\]**: Keep the changes from one branch (shows the "
"actual branch name, like \"main\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:190
msgid ""
"**Use \\[other-branch\\]**: Keep the changes from the other branch (like "
"\"feature-branch\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:191
msgid ""
"**Use Both**: Keep both sets of changes, with your branch's changes first"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:193
msgid ""
"Click a button to resolve that conflict. The conflict markers are removed "
"and replaced with your chosen content. After resolving all conflicts in a "
"file, stage it and commit to complete the merge."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:195
msgid ""
"**Tip:** For complex conflicts that need manual editing, you can edit the "
"file directly. Remove the conflict markers (`<<<<<<<`, `=======`, `>>>>>>>`) "
"and keep the content you want."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:197
msgid "Stashing"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:199
msgid ""
"Git stash allows you to temporarily save your uncommitted changes and revert "
"your working directory to a clean state. This is particularly useful when "
"you need to quickly switch branches or pull updates without committing "
"incomplete work."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:201
msgid "Creating Stashes"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:203
msgid ""
"To stash all your current changes, use the <code class=\"hljs\">git: stash "
"all</code> action. This will save both staged and unstaged changes to a new "
"stash entry and clean your working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:205
msgid "Managing Stashes"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:207
msgid ""
"Zed provides a stash picker accessible via <code class=\"hljs\">git: view "
"stash</code> or from the Git Panel's overflow menu. From the stash picker, "
"you can:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:209
msgid ""
"**View stash list**: Browse all your saved stashes with their descriptions "
"and timestamps"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:210
msgid "**Open diffs**: See exactly what changes are stored in each stash"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:211
msgid ""
"**Apply stashes**: Apply stash changes to your working directory while "
"keeping the stash entry"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:212
msgid ""
"**Pop stashes**: Apply stash changes and remove the stash entry from the list"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:213
msgid "**Drop stashes**: Delete unwanted stash entries without applying them"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:215
msgid "Quick Stash Operations"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:217
msgid ""
"For faster workflows, Zed provides direct actions to work with the most "
"recent stash:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:219
msgid ""
"**Apply latest stash**: Use <code class=\"hljs\">git: stash apply</code> to "
"apply the most recent stash without removing it"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:220
msgid ""
"**Pop latest stash**: Use <code class=\"hljs\">git: stash pop</code> to "
"apply and remove the most recent stash"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:222
msgid "Stash Diff View"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:224
msgid ""
"To view a stash's contents, select it in the stash picker and press <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-shift-v\\|ctrl-shift-v</kbd>. From the diff view, "
"you can use these keybindings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:226 src/git.md:316
msgid "Action"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:226 src/git.md:316
msgid "Keybinding"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:228
msgid "Apply stash"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:228
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-space\\|ctrl-space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:229
msgid "Pop stash (apply and remove)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:229
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-shift-space\\|ctrl-shift-space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:230
msgid "Drop stash (remove without applying)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:230
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-shift-backspace\\|ctrl-shift-backspace</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:232
msgid "AI Support in Git"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:234
msgid ""
"Zed currently supports LLM-powered commit message generation. You can ask AI "
"to generate a commit message by focusing on the message editor within the "
"Git Panel and either clicking on the pencil icon in the bottom left, or "
"reaching for the <code class=\"hljs\">git: generate commit message</code> "
"(<kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-tab\\|alt-l</kbd>) keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:237
msgid ""
"Note that you need to have an LLM provider configured either via your own "
"API keys or through Zed's hosted AI models. Visit [the AI configuration page]"
"(./ai/configuration.md) to learn how to do so."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:240
msgid ""
"You can specify your preferred model to use by providing a "
"`commit_message_model` agent setting. See [Feature-specific models](./ai/"
"agent-settings.md#feature-specific-models) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:245
msgid "\"agent\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:246
msgid "\"commit_message_model\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:247 src/git.md:282
msgid "\"provider\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:247
msgid "\"anthropic\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:248
msgid "\"model\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:248
msgid "\"claude-3-5-haiku\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:254
msgid ""
"To customize the format of generated commit messages, run <code "
"class=\"hljs\">agent: open rules library</code> and select the \"Commit "
"message\" rule on the left side. From there, you can modify the prompt to "
"match your desired format."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:259
msgid ""
"Any specific instructions for commit messages added to [Rules files](./ai/"
"rules.md) are also picked up by the model tasked with writing your commit "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:261
msgid "Git Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:263
msgid ""
"Zed integrates with popular Git hosting services to ensure that Git commit "
"hashes and references to Issues, Pull Requests, and Merge Requests become "
"clickable links."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:265
msgid ""
"Zed currently supports links to the hosted versions of [GitHub](https://"
"github.com), [GitLab](https://gitlab.com), [Bitbucket](https://bitbucket."
"org), [SourceHut](https://sr.ht) and [Codeberg](https://codeberg.org)."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:272
msgid "Self-Hosted Instances"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:274
msgid ""
"Zed automatically identifies Git hosting providers by checking for keywords "
"in your Git remote URL. For example, if your self-hosted URL contains "
"`gitlab`, `gitea`, or other recognized provider names, Zed will "
"automatically register that hosting provider without any configuration "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:276
msgid ""
"However, if your self-hosted Git instance URL doesn't contain identifying "
"keywords, you can manually configure Zed to create clickable links to your "
"instance by adding a `git_hosting_providers` setting so commit hashes and "
"permalinks resolve to your domain:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:280
msgid "\"git_hosting_providers\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:282
msgid "\"gitlab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:283
msgid "\"name\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:283
msgid "\"Corp GitLab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:284
msgid "\"base_url\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:284
msgid "\"https://git.example.corp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:290
msgid ""
"The `provider` field specifies which type of hosting service you're using. "
"Supported `provider` values are `github`, `gitlab`, `bitbucket`, `gitea`, "
"`forgejo`, and `sourcehut`. The `name` is optional and used as a display "
"name for your instance, and `base_url` is the root URL of your self-hosted "
"server."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:292
msgid ""
"You can configure multiple custom providers if you work with several self-"
"hosted instances."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:294
msgid "Permalinks"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:296
msgid ""
"Zed also has a Copy Permalink feature to create a permanent link to a code "
"snippet on your Git hosting service. These links are useful for sharing a "
"specific line or range of lines in a file at a specific commit. Trigger this "
"action via the [Command Palette](./getting-started.md#command-palette) "
"(search for `permalink`), by creating a [custom key bindings](key-bindings."
"md#custom-key-bindings) to the `editor::CopyPermalinkToLine` or `editor::"
"OpenPermalinkToLine` actions or by simply right clicking and selecting `Copy "
"Permalink` with line(s) selected in your editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:303
msgid "Diff Hunk Keyboard Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:305
msgid ""
"When viewing files with changes, Zed displays diff hunks that can be "
"expanded or collapsed for detailed review:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:307
msgid ""
"**Expand all diff hunks**: <code class=\"hljs\">editor: expand all diff "
"hunks</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-\"\\|ctrl-\"</kbd>)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:308
msgid ""
"**Collapse all diff hunks**: Press `Escape` (bound to <code "
"class=\"hljs\">editor: cancel</code>)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:309
msgid ""
"**Toggle selected diff hunks**: <code class=\"hljs\">editor: toggle selected "
"diff hunks</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-'\\|ctrl-'</kbd>)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:310
msgid ""
"**Navigate between hunks**: <code class=\"hljs\">editor: go to hunk</code> "
"and <code class=\"hljs\">editor: go to previous hunk</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:312
msgid ""
"**Tip:** The `Escape` key is the quickest way to collapse all expanded diff "
"hunks and return to an overview of your changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:314
msgid "Action Reference"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:318
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: add</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:318 src/git.md:334 src/git.md:335 src/git.md:336 src/git.md:338
#: src/git.md:339 src/git.md:340 src/git.md:341 src/git.md:342
msgid "<div>No default binding</div>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:319
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: stage all</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:319
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-ctrl-y\\|ctrl-space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:320
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: unstage all</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:320
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-ctrl-shift-y\\|ctrl-shift-space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:321
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: toggle staged</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:321
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">space\\|space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:322
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: stage and next</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:322
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-y\\|alt-y</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:323
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: unstage and next</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:323
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-y\\|alt-shift-y</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:324
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: commit</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:324
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter\\|ctrl-enter</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:325
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">git: expand commit editor</code>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:325
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-escape\\|</kbd>"
msgstr ""

